      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with 4 cm of fresh snow overnight setting up a nice clear start before snow flurries and strong northwest winds build through the day, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently -3°C with winds around 32 km/h gusting to 60 km/h. Grooming has laid down fresh cord over the new snow, with variable off-piste conditions, pockets of wind-drifted snow and some wind-stripped patches. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, Captains Express, T-Bar and Wells Pipe Platter are all open, with McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express and Valley View on wind hold, and Soho Express and Willow's Quad closed for the day due to increasing winds; 5 of 10 lifts are currently running. Patrol is conducting avalanche mitigation work this morning, with slight delays possible in Willows and Soho; the Olympic Pipe closes at 11:45am. (Issued: 12:08pm, 22 Sep) The access road is chain-free but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory in place; the morning was the best window today, with the Upper Clutha Primary Schools Race running in Captains this morning. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 5 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
