      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with spring funkiness continuing and timing being everything. Overnight precipitation, a mix of rain and snow, left things firm this morning, with overnight wind blowing away much of the new snow, though the sun has since softened things up into another fun, springy day; the natural base holds at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin. It's currently -2°C with winds around 26 km/h gusting to 43 km/h, with more weather and snow showers forecast to move in later. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter are all open, all 3 of 3 lifts running, with 6 of 9 terrain zones open including Home Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes and the terrain park; Powder Bowl and Matukituki Basin are delayed, and Motatapu Chutes is closed. Skiers are advised to get to Saddle Basin early, as Saddle Track access is likely to close late morning, though the Saddle lift will keep running for those already out there. Backcountry and skinning access are both open; the access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
